Fixes https://github.com/hyperledger/solang/issues/1283.

Allow sol and lamports to be used as units
    
This removes the ether, wei, gwei, seconds, days, weeks, hours, and minutes keywords.
   
```solidity 
contract foo {
      int value = 10 sol;
}
```
The parser has been modified to parse any identifier after a number literal  as a unit, but to make the parser unambiguouos some errors cases are not handled as well, no worse than solc though. In many cases where number literals are not expected, they are no longer parsed and will result in a parse error rather than a parse tree which would never resolve anyway. For example:
    
    function foo(1 bar)
    (1 + 2) days    
    emit 1(foo);

Are all parse errors now. 
    
